![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

If `with_worker_api_key` is called with an invalid key, it silently ignores the error and builds a client without the `Authorization` header. Since this method is explicitly called to configure the API key, it should fail fast by panicking if the key is invalid.

```suggestion
    pub fn with_worker_api_key(key: &str) -> Self {
        let mut headers = reqwest::header::HeaderMap::new();
        let mut v = reqwest::header::HeaderValue::from_str(&format!("Bearer {key}"))
            .expect("invalid worker API key format");
        v.set_sensitive(true);
        headers.insert(reqwest::header::AUTHORIZATION, v);
        let client = reqwest::Client::builder()
            .timeout(SERVER_INFO_TIMEOUT)
            .default_headers(headers)
            .build()
            .expect("introspector http client builds");
        Self { client }
    }
```

